    "rubric": "A nine-year-old AND a grandparent both know the word; a thing you'd chat about, not an encyclopedia heading; mid-connectivity nouns, no mega-hubs; no near-duplicates. Register calibrated to Gray's examples: Roses, WWII, Coffee, Baseball, Paul McCartney, Eiffel Tower, Halloween, Chess, Harry Potter, Apollo 11, Dracula, Superman, Lego, Pizza, Vikings, Surfing, Jazz.",
