    "topicsPerDomain": "15-27 (21 in the first authoring wave; wave 2 added 55 high-traffic replacements skewed to the domains the 20k gate hit hardest — the gate drops generic everyday objects, so replacements lean famous entities: people, works, brands, places)",
    "count": 475,
    "note": "Titles are best-guess canonical; the resolve pass (canonicalize via &redirects, 404-drop, 20k views/month gate, post-canonical dedupe) produces data/topics-annotated.json, whose in-pool survivors are the sampling pool."
